 "notes": [
  "Pool index is (target cell c, target deficit hour h_c); candidate trips end at j!=c within 450 m and are counted in the arrivals at j in h_c. Same-cell redirections are excluded (0 edges). The removed same-cell units are 34.110% of the naive pair pool, which reproduces the old 34.105% path as an audit figure, not a result.",
  "One reroute per trip is enforced by sum_c x[j,c,h] <= A[j,h]. The naive pair pool is 334,147.32 units vs 307,187.50 distinct source-hour units (ratio 1.0878, the M8 1.09); the LP resolves it, so q(r*) = 95,565.82 <= distinct.",
  "The old 2.93 ratio is reproduced as 334,147.32/113,936 = 2.9328; the difference comes from the old source-own-deficit-hour count, not from the new target-hour pool.",
  "Targeted upper bound (bound=upper_no_source_deficit, source capacity = full arrivals A[j,h_c]): r*=1.76 CNY, q*=95,565.82 (44.17% of N), bill 168,195.84, truck residual 402,253.15, total 570,448.99 vs 720,536.87 all-truck, saving 20.83% at TRUCK_UNIT=3.3305. This is an upper bound because a source with no hourly surplus is allowed to donate a bike.",
  "Conservative bound (bound=hourly_surplus_sources, source capacity = max(0, arr-dep)): r*=1.83 CNY, q*=32,777.11 (15.15% of N), bill 59,982.12, truck residual 611,372.09, total 671,354.21 vs 720,536.87, saving 6.826%. It matches the R1 reference r*=1.83, q*=32,777.11 and 6.826% within 1e-4. Every source hour has enough surplus to cover the reroutes it supplies.",
  "Zone decomposition at each bound's own r*: targeted cross-zone 7,133.35 (7.464% of q), positive zone-hour sum 4,332.11, max |zone-hour| 327.83, 19 zones flip between deficit and surplus; conservative cross-zone 2,836.57 (8.654%), positive sum 2,315.70, max 273.45, 10 zones flip.",
  "The 14-row interval (7 kappa/rho/c0 sets x 2 truck units) covers acceptance and truck-cost uncertainty only. It does not cover the source-cap assumption, so the upper and conservative bounds are separate scenarios, not two ends of that interval.",
  "Public push with the corrected unit is not profitable: the optimum is r=0 (saving 0). At r=1.2 it loses 0.22% while paying 120,049.55 to free riders; with the historical unit 3.478 it saves 0.98%, not the old 2.1% (that figure used a non-flow pool). All three are reported so T012 can state the lower bound honestly.",
  "The free-rider count is 100,041.29 existing non-same-cell arrivals into target cells in their deficit hours; targeted push pays zero free riders by construction.",
  "Acceptance parameters are not identified from May 2017 (no reward was offered); the 7-set x 2-unit sweep is the interval. TRUCK_UNIT is final from T007: 3.3305 main, 1.8718 lower; the old 3.478 is obsolete except as a historical comparison.",
  "Text-code consistency: the section's 'in c's deficit hour' is now what the code does; the old source-own-hour path is gone.",
  "No paper/review/data file outside data/runs/T008 is written."
 ],
